    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0213" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg125"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr.
                            Wharton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1562.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    summer in China so far has been quiet, and no serious antiforeign riots have
                    occurred. There are indications, however, that the conspirators in Hu-Nan are
                    again endeavoring to stir up popular prejudice. The circulation of placards
                    containing abuse of foreigners and missionaries has again commenced. It appears
                    that these placards were prepared in Hu-Nan and were sent to Chang-tel-Fu, a
                    city in the province of Hu-Nan.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith copies of four of these placards.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d95-a1.xml" xpointer="d95-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
